    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.5, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"U4\"], \"pins\": [\"U4.10\", \"U4.11\", \"U4.12\"], \"nets\": [\"VCC\", \"GND\"], \"observed\": \"On the display sheet, the BS0 pin (pin 10) appears to be wired to the top horizontal VCC wire (the same wire that feeds the R4, R6 and R7 pull-ups), not to GND. BS1 (pin 11) and BS2 (pin 12) appear to go to the GND branch near the GND symbol at the right of U4. The strapping therefore does not match the 0,1,0 pattern.\", \"expected\": \"Specification: \\\"BS0 (pin 10) \u2192 GND, BS1 (pin 11) \u2192 VCC, BS2 (pin 12) \u2192 GND\\\", i.e. BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 for the I2C configuration the display is meant to use.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`BS0` (pin 10) \u2192 GND; `BS1` (pin 11) \u2192 VCC; `BS2` (pin 12) \u2192 GND. That BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 strapping ... is the SSD1306's documented I2C-mode pin configuration\"}, {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"display.kicad_sch: BS0 10 / BS1 11 / BS2 12 pins; the top VCC wire at y\u2248310 runs from the VCC symbol to pin 10 and to the R4/R6/R7 pull-ups, while the GND symbol at right connects to the BS1/BS2 branch\"}], \"impact\": \"The SSD1306 would latch a different interface mode from the one the firmware expects (I2C). The OLED would likely fail to respond on the DISP_SCL/DISP_SDA bus, so the display would not work.\", \"confidence\": 0.5}]}",
